From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kiritantakechi <kiritantakechi@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 08:45:15 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] libbpf, bpftool: check the BTF's raw data before cloning it

Add a package patch to libbpf and to bpftool, whose source carries its
own libbpf: bpf_object__sanitize_and_load_btf passes the result of
btf__raw_data to btf__new unchecked, and when the raw data cannot be
allocated, btf__new copies an indeterminate number of bytes from NULL.
Return -ENOMEM instead, as libbpf has done since its commit
fd04b4eae1a3, which no release carries yet.

Found reviewing the -O3 build's warnings of bpftool: 'sz' may be used
uninitialized (-Wmaybe-uninitialized), where libbpf's own package, whose
functions are not inlined into each other, has no warning.

Signed-off-by: kiritantakechi <kiritantakechi@gmail.com>
Upstream-Status: Backport [libbpf fd04b4eae1a3, part of "libbpf: Support sanitization of BTF layout for older kernels"]
---
 package/libs/libbpf/Makefile                  |  2 +-
 ...the-BTF-s-raw-data-before-cloning-it.patch | 24 +++++++++++++++++++
 package/network/utils/bpftool/Makefile        |  2 +-
 ...the-BTF-s-raw-data-before-cloning-it.patch | 24 +++++++++++++++++++
 4 files changed, 50 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 package/libs/libbpf/patches/010-libbpf-check-the-BTF-s-raw-data-before-cloning-it.patch
 create mode 100644 package/network/utils/bpftool/patches/010-libbpf-check-the-BTF-s-raw-data-before-cloning-it.patch

diff --git a/package/libs/libbpf/Makefile b/package/libs/libbpf/Makefile
index c5cb4e1..d67c7c4 100644
--- a/package/libs/libbpf/Makefile
+++ b/package/libs/libbpf/Makefile
@@ -9,7 +9,7 @@ include $(TOPDIR)/rules.mk
 
 PKG_NAME:=libbpf
 PKG_VERSION:=1.7.0
-PKG_RELEASE:=1
+PKG_RELEASE:=2
 
 PKG_SOURCE_URL:=https://github.com/libbpf/libbpf
 PKG_MIRROR_HASH:=30fbb65adcb4ce7e5eac797edbb81ede5e00969f8eb6a871b9e7913eda4e8ba4
diff --git a/package/libs/libbpf/patches/010-libbpf-check-the-BTF-s-raw-data-before-cloning-it.patch b/package/libs/libbpf/patches/010-libbpf-check-the-BTF-s-raw-data-before-cloning-it.patch
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..818f82d
--- /dev/null
+++ b/package/libs/libbpf/patches/010-libbpf-check-the-BTF-s-raw-data-before-cloning-it.patch
@@ -0,0 +1,24 @@
+From: kiritantakechi <kiritantakechi@gmail.com>
+Subject: [PATCH] libbpf: check the BTF's raw data before cloning it
+
+bpf_object__sanitize_and_load_btf clones the object's BTF before it
+sanitizes it, and passes the result of btf__raw_data to btf__new
+unchecked. When btf__raw_data cannot allocate the raw data, it returns
+NULL and leaves the size unset, and btf__new copies an indeterminate
+number of bytes from NULL. Return -ENOMEM instead, as libbpf's commit
+fd04b4eae1a3 ("libbpf: Support sanitization of BTF layout for older
+kernels") does where it moved the clone.
+
+Signed-off-by: kiritantakechi <kiritantakechi@gmail.com>
+---
+--- a/src/libbpf.c
++++ b/src/libbpf.c
+@@ -3605,6 +3605,8 @@ static int bpf_object__sanitize_and_load_btf(struct bpf_object *obj)
+ 
+ 		/* clone BTF to sanitize a copy and leave the original intact */
+ 		raw_data = btf__raw_data(obj->btf, &sz);
++		if (!raw_data)
++			return -ENOMEM;
+ 		kern_btf = btf__new(raw_data, sz);
+ 		err = libbpf_get_error(kern_btf);
+ 		if (err)
